WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.502 --> 00:00:03.003
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.706
You’re here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:07.674
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.043
Well, guys, the Super Bowl
is just a few days away,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.079
and people are getting
really excited.

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:13.413
Maybe -- Maybe too excited.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:17.017
A new poll found that a record
68 million Americans

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.454
will be making some kind
of bet on the big game.

00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:21.889
Yeah, which is tough for me,

00:00:21.889 --> 00:00:23.824
'cause I already bet
it wouldn’t go over 60 million.

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:27.861
So...I’m already --
I’m already down.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.463
I knew betting was getting
out of hand this morning,

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:31.265
when my daughter asked me
to put her college fund

00:00:31.265 --> 00:00:33.200
in a DraftKings account.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.869
"Don't worry.
I’m gonna double it, alright?"

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.205
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:41.508
"Are you smoking?"
"Who are you, the police?"

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.577
But actually, I saw
some other interesting polls

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:44.578
about the Super Bowl.

00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:45.679
Look at this one here...

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.224
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.224 --> 00:00:59.626
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.329
That's --

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:03.564
Here’s another poll I liked...

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.544
Oh.
Larry. Larry.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.479
-Larry, of course.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.514
-And finally...

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.455
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.790
What?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.991
A deli--

00:01:30.991 --> 00:01:32.559
[ Laughs ]

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.928
-Wow.
-Wow!

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.264
Meanwhile, it’s been crazy
here in New York City

00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:40.868
'cause President Biden
has been in town all day.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.903
Yeah, and just one minute
on the subway

00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:44.938
was all it took to end
his love of trains.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.608
He’s like, "That’s it.
Good Lord."

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:48.909
Biden had fun
while he was here.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:51.211
He even took a horse and buggy
around Central Park,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.980
or as he calls it, Uber.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.684
And New Yorkers were actually
very excited for Biden.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:00.087
It’s rare that we get
to see a president in town

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:02.456
who’s not walking in and out of
a courthouse, don’t you think?

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:04.191
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.191 --> 00:02:06.260
It’s nice to see, refreshing.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.396
But the big story today is that

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:13.100
Republican National Committee
Chairwoman Ronna McDaniel

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.902
appears to be stepping down

00:02:14.902 --> 00:02:17.538
due to pressure
from former President Trump.

00:02:17.538 --> 00:02:20.440
Yeah, McDaniel says she wants
to work someplace more stable,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.909
like Boeing or Twitter.

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:25.212
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:25.212 --> 00:02:26.813
Apparently, Trump
has been disappointed

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.382
with the RNC’s finances.

00:02:28.382 --> 00:02:30.918
He was like, "They’re wasting
all their money on my lawyers.

00:02:30.918 --> 00:02:33.420
Sad."

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.721
Looks like McDaniel
will leave

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.090
after the South Carolina
primary.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.292
Nikki Haley heard and was like,

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:41.328
"Hey, want to
split a cab home?"

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:43.764
Yeah, that’s right,
RNC Chairwoman Ronna McDaniel

00:02:43.764 --> 00:02:45.732
has told Trump
that she plans to step down.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.634
That’s big news
for the Republican Party.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.304
And based on Trump’s statement,
it’s really affected him.

00:02:50.304 --> 00:02:52.673
Here’s what he had to say about
Ronna McDaniel stepping down.

00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:53.874
Said...

00:03:07.821 --> 00:03:08.989
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:11.959
No, no, no.
No, no.

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:13.493
Ronna McDaniel.

00:03:15.162 --> 00:03:16.530
Some more political news.

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.498
Last night, House Republicans
tried to impeach

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:21.668
Homeland Security Secretary
Alejandro Mayorkas,

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.871
but they didn’t have
enough votes.

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.939
If you don’t know Mayorkas,
here he is.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.775
Yeah, well, a lot of lawmakers
spoke out to defend him.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.043
-Really?
-Yeah. For instance,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.745
Congressman Keith Self said...

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.318
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.053
And Congressman
Brian Mast said...

00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:47.528
Then Congressman
Greg Landsman said...

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.401
And congressmen Andre Carson,
William Timmons,

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:56.069
and Chip Roy all said...

00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:00.908
Congressman Mike Garcia said...

00:04:03.544 --> 00:04:05.379
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:07.748
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.952 --> 00:04:13.754
Congressman Mike Rogers said...

00:04:17.024 --> 00:04:18.759
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.866
And finally, Congressman
Chuck Edwards said...

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.771
You can see --
At least you see some support.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.308
Some news from overseas.

00:04:34.308 --> 00:04:35.709
Today, the Kremlin confirmed

00:04:35.709 --> 00:04:39.847
that Tucker Carlson
has interviewed Vladimir Putin.

00:04:39.847 --> 00:04:41.315
You can tell the interview
went over well

00:04:41.315 --> 00:04:42.950
'cause Tucker is still alive.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.952
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:46.386
Apparently Putin
was a good host.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.288
He was like,
"What would you like to drink?

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.357
Tap poison or bottled poison?"

00:04:50.357 --> 00:04:52.226
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:04:52.226 --> 00:04:54.394
"Which one would you --"

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.297
Yep, Tucker Carlson
interviewing Vladimir Putin

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.832
may not mean much to you,

00:04:58.832 --> 00:05:01.235
but for Trump,
this is like watching OnlyFans.

00:05:01.235 --> 00:05:04.071
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.071 --> 00:05:07.207
[ As Trump ] This is insane.

00:05:07.207 --> 00:05:08.475
[ Normal voice ]
Well, some business news.

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:10.010
I heard that amid low sales,

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.013
the head of Fisher-Price
is being replaced.

00:05:13.013 --> 00:05:14.615
Yeah.

00:05:14.615 --> 00:05:17.584
Even worse, he received
the bad news on this.

00:05:17.584 --> 00:05:19.953
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.089 --> 00:05:23.090
Listen to this.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.491
I read that a man
who spent years

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:26.260
building a model
of the Eiffel Tower

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.197
with 700,000 matchsticks
has been denied the world record

00:05:30.197 --> 00:05:32.299
'cause he used
the wrong kind of matches.

00:05:32.299 --> 00:05:35.302
-Aw! Come on.

00:05:35.302 --> 00:05:36.403
-That’s what you want to do,

00:05:36.403 --> 00:05:39.106
upset a guy
with 700,000 matchsticks?

00:05:39.106 --> 00:05:40.207
Burn the city down.

00:05:40.207 --> 00:05:41.508
On the bright side,

00:05:41.508 --> 00:05:44.178
he did set a record for longest
scream of frustration.

00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:46.046
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.046 --> 00:05:47.981
And finally, a man in Florida
was arrested

00:05:47.981 --> 00:05:50.017
after he showed up
to the airport fully naked

00:05:50.017 --> 00:05:52.753
and tried to walk past security.

00:05:52.753 --> 00:05:54.087
And since he was detained,

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.390
Southwest had to find
another pilot.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:00.060
We have a great show tonight.
Carey Mulligan is here.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.530
Oscar-nominated Carey Mulligan.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.199
Alan Cumming is joining us.

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:07.067
Ooh, "Traitors."

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:10.037
And we got great music
from Idles.

00:06:10.037 --> 00:06:11.505
Stick around.

00:06:11.505 --> 00:06:14.041
We're playing a fun new game
when we come back, brand-new.

00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.108
Come on back, now.

